/-!
# A cartesian `𝒪_F`-module is generated by its sections over an affine étale chart

Let `F` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S` contained in a big fppf site `B` and let `G` be
an `𝒪_F`-module on the small étale site of `F` which is *cartesian on affine charts*
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsCartesianOnAffineCharts`): the sections over a smaller affine chart
are the base change of the sections over a larger one.  This file proves that such a module is
**generated by its sections over an affine chart**: for an affine étale chart `V` the canonical
morphism from the coproduct of copies of `𝒪_F|_V` indexed by `G(V)` to `G|_V` is an
epimorphism of modules on the slice of the small étale site at `V`.

This is the *generators* half of one direction of Descent, Proposition 03DX(2) — the direction
asserting that a module cartesian on affine charts is quasi-coherent on the site.  The other
half, the *relations*, is not proved here; see the implementation notes for exactly what is
owed, and `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_rel`
for the resulting reduction.

## Main definitions

* `SheafOfModules.liftUnitPresentation` is the structure sheaf with its sections raised to the
  universe in which `SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation` takes its coproducts, for modules with
  sections in an arbitrary universe, and `SheafOfModules.liftSectionHomPresentation` is the
  morphism out of it determined by a global section.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGeneratorsSource` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGenerators` are the coproduct of copies of
  `SheafOfModules.liftUnitPresentation` of the slice at the chart, indexed by the sections of `G`
  over the chart, and the canonical morphism from it to the universe lift
  `SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation` of the restriction of `G`.  The leg at a section is
  `SheafOfModules.liftSectionHomPresentation` of the global section of the restriction that the
  section determines.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.freeChartCover` is the same construction in Mathlib's
  `SheafOfModules.free` vocabulary, at the module universe of the schemes, with
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mkOver` as its family of sections.

## Main results

* `Stacks.PresheafOfModules.isLocallySurjective_of_surjective_of_isCoverDense`: a morphism of
  presheaves of modules which is surjective on the sections over the objects in the image of a
  cover-dense functor is locally surjective.
* `SheafOfModules.hasGlobalPresentation_of_epi_kernelLift`: **the assembly lemma.**  An
  epimorphism onto a module from a coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf, whose kernel
  receives an epimorphism from a second such coproduct, is a global presentation.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCoverDense_affineChartsOver`: the affine étale charts over a chart
  `V` are cover-dense in the slice of the small étale site at `V`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasiCompactObject_over_of_isAffine`: an object of a slice of the
  small étale site whose underlying chart is affine is a quasi-compact object of that slice.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.surjective_chartGenerators_app` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_chartGenerators`: **a module cartesian on affine charts is
  generated by its sections over an affine chart.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_freeChartCover`: the same statement for Mathlib's
  `SheafOfModules.free`, at the module universe of the schemes, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGeneratingSections`, which packages it as Mathlib's
  `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_rel`: the
  reduction of the cartesian-implies-quasi-coherent direction of Descent, Proposition 03DX(2)
  to the relations half.

## Implementation notes

**Two module universes appear and they are not the same.** The predicate
`SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.QuasicoherentOnSite` takes its coproducts and its
cokernel at the universe `max u v r m` of the site objects, the site morphisms, the coefficient
rings and the module sections. On a slice of the small étale site of an algebraic space over
`Scheme.{u}` that universe is `max (u + 1) m` for an `𝒪_F`-module in
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.Modules B S hS F hF` with sections in the universe `m`, which is arbitrary
here, while the coefficient rings are in `u`. Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.free` exists only when the
index, the coefficient rings and the module sections share one universe, so it cannot produce the
coproducts a presentation needs. The coproducts are therefore taken abstractly, of copies of
`SheafOfModules.liftUnitPresentation`, and the morphisms out of them are computed by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.uliftUnitHomEquiv` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.InternalHomFreeBaseCase`, which is the universe-lifted form
of Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.unitHomEquiv`. Both forms of the generation statement are recorded:
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_chartGenerators` at the presentation universe, which is the one a
presentation can use, and `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_freeChartCover` in the `SheafOfModules.free`
vocabulary at the module universe `u`.

Sheafification of `AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) m}`-valued presheaves on a slice of the small étale
site, and the identification of its local equivalences with the locally bijective morphisms, are
carried as instance hypotheses rather than declared as instances:
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.hasSheafify_over_presentationUniverse` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.wEqualsLocallyBijective_over_presentationUniverse` discharge them. The
tree already carries the two corresponding facts at `AddCommGrpCat.{u}` as instances, and a second
pair at `AddCommGrpCat.{max (u + 1) m}` would leave instance search with two candidates for a value
universe that is still a metavariable, which is how the universe constraints in this area become
unsolvable; `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.hasSheafify_smallEtaleRingedSite_addCommGrpCat` is a theorem
and not an instance for the same reason.

**What remains to be supplied.**  A global
presentation of `G|_V` is a cokernel of a map between two coproducts of copies of the structure
sheaf.  The first coproduct and the epimorphism out of it are
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGenerators` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_chartGenerators`, proved here from
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsCartesianOnAffineCharts` alone.  The second — that the *relations*
among those generators are again generated by global ones — is the hypothesis `hrel` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_rel`.  Its
mathematical content is that the kernel of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartGenerators` is
cartesian between the affine objects of the slice, which needs

* the sections of a coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf over an affine object of the
  *slice* site, that is, `Stacks.Sites.sheafOfModules_sections_preserves_coproducts` (Stacks
  0935) applied at a quasi-compact object of the slice — the quasi-compactness half of which is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasiCompactObject_over_of_isAffine`, proved here, and the
  comparison half of which is the analogue of `Stacks.Sites.bijective_freeSectionsMap` for a
  coproduct of copies of `SheafOfModules.liftUnit`, which is not;
* the slice analogue of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_free`, at the
  presentation universe; and
* the slice analogue of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_kernel`, whose
  content is flatness of the restriction maps between affine charts
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.flat_chartRestrict_of_isAffine`, which *is* available) together with
  exactness of base change along a flat ring map.

So the residue is the chart-sections toolkit of this tree — `ChartSections`,
`FreeModuleSections`, `FreeModuleCartesian`, `ChartSectionsKernel` — redone for a *slice* of the
small étale site at the presentation universe.  None of Descent 03DV, Descent 0GN7 or right
exactness of the associated-module functor, the three inputs that the other direction of
Descent, Proposition 03DX(2) needs and which this tree does not have, is used anywhere in this
file or in the residue above.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is claimed anywhere.  Descent, Proposition 03DX(2) is an equivalence of
categories and belongs to the Descent chapter (Chapter 35); the conventions of the
sibling files `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.FreeModuleCartesian` and
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.SliceAssociatedModuleEssSurj` — no tag on a conditional
statement, and no tag on a statement of another chapter's result — are followed.

